## Reference kernels hoisted from FBCIR_code (Andreou and Chen, 2026), the
## backward causal influence range. Same mechanism as extracts.dcf: `Lines`
## addresses the UNMODIFIED reference script in matlab_reference_fbcir/,
## tools/extract.R copies the range byte for byte, and check_extraction fails
## on a byte of drift. Reference commit f9fe922 (2026-07-27), MIT.
##
## Gate G1 for these records runs against the script's own workspace saved
## from a complete, unmodified run (N = 22000 completes in about 190 s on base
## MATLAB, so no problem-size knob is needed).

Function: ref_backward_cir_tipping
Script: climate_tipping_y_bifurcation_driven.m
Lines: 939-1277
Provenance: the reference implementation of Andreou and Chen (FBCIR_code) | Copyright (c) 2026 Marios Andreou
Inputs: CIR_epsilon_values, E_j_matrices, F_j_matrices, L_x, L_y, N,
 RE_metric_threshold, back_lag_time_end_plot,
 calculate_and_plot_exact_objective_backward_CIR,
 calculate_and_plot_normalised_backward_CIR_metric, dt, eps_ord_values, f_x,
 f_y, filter_cov, filter_mean, first_idx, gamma, plot_len, target_last_idx, x
Outputs: back_subjective_CIR, back_approx_objective_CIR,
 back_defn_objective_CIR, back_max_RE_metric, back_RE_metric_mask,
 adaptive_approx_objective_backward_CIR_n, lag_bound, back_plot_len,
 back_lag_steps
Pairs: aci_range(direction = "backward")
Note: The whole BACKWARD CIR section of the bifurcation-driven tipping script,
 from the first code line after the section banner to the line before the
 plotting section: the adaptive-lag online smoother run backward from every
 observational time, the centred complete backward CIR metric, the subjective
 backward range over the 513 epsilon thresholds, the objective backward range
 by the Theorem 1 approximation and by the definition (Simpson over epsilon),
 and the validity gate (back_max_RE_metric against RE_metric_threshold). The
 section consumes the forward section's online-smoother auxiliaries
 (E_j_matrices, F_j_matrices) and the filter, so those are inputs rather than
 recomputed. lag_bound is the literal N inside the slice, as the script sets
 it. The inputs and outputs were derived mechanically from the slice against
 the saved workspace on 2026-08-28.
